  "style_bible": "A unified symbolic psychological illustration language: high-contrast hand-drawn ink on an off-white paper field, deep charcoal-black shadows, thick expressive brush contours, restrained chalk-line human figures, sparse compositions, and one controlled warm gold accent #FFD700 used only to signify an unacknowledged possibility or perceived success. Use continuous tableaux rather than panels, split screens, collages, or explanatory diagrams. Favor readable silhouettes, strong negative space, quiet atmospheric ink fades, and emotionally legible gestures at television-grid size. Symbolic scenes are editorial illustrations, never evidence, diagnosis, literal memory, or factual reconstruction. Keep all generated visuals completely text-free: no Japanese characters, English letters, numbers, logos, labels, interface text, books, notes, signs, or readable screens. Maintain visual continuity through recurring window boundaries, projected shadows, chest knots, reflected silhouettes, and transitions from dense black ink toward narrow gold openings. Avoid photorealism, celebrity resemblance, detailed facial features, colorful palettes, glossy rendering, decorative clutter, literal trophies, medical imagery, and melodramatic crying.",
  "character_bible": "The recurring fictional chalk-line figure is an anonymous adult Japanese silhouette with a round unfeatured head, slim neutral proportions, restrained dot eyes only when necessary, simple off-white ink lines, black or charcoal clothing blocks, and thick consistent brush contours. The figure has no identifiable age, hairstyle, celebrity resemblance, or distinctive personal features. Preserve the same head silhouette, body proportions, line weight, charcoal/off-white treatment, and understated posture in every appearance. Emotional states must be communicated through small physical actions: a thin polite smile, shoulders held rigid, one hand pressing a dense black knot over the chest, hesitation before reaching toward light, turning away from or toward a window, or standing beside an enlarged shadow. The shadow may become oversized and expressive, but it remains visually connected to the figure and is never a separate named character. When another person is needed, use only an anonymous simplified silhouette with no facial detail; distinguish perceived success through controlled gold illumination rather than trophies, awards, clothing, or text.",
  "environment_bible": "Use recurring threshold environments built around a large window as the central symbolic boundary between the visible social world and the private inner world. Interiors are sparse and abstract: dark charcoal walls, off-white paper texture, soft window light, empty floor planes, and occasional indistinct architectural edges. Exteriors should remain minimal, often a pale or charcoal atmospheric field containing one anonymous silhouette touched by a narrow pool of warm gold. The window may function as glass, a frame, a reflection surface, or a psychological aperture, but it must remain one integrated spatial element rather than a literal two-panel composition. Shadows can cross the sill, stretch across walls, overlap the figure, or reach toward the gold opening to visualize shadow and denied possibility. Reuse the same window proportions, charcoal value range, off-white paper grain, and single-gold-accent rule throughout the video. Keep environments text-free and remove all readable objects, screens, documents, signs, calendars, books, phones, desks, trophies, and interface elements.",
  "opening_visual_contract": {
    "thumbnail_scene": "A continuous ink tableau of the recurring chalk-line figure inside a large window boundary, maintaining a thin polite smile while pressing one hand over a dense black knot in the chest. An oversized shadow reaches toward an anonymous silhouette outside, which is touched by one controlled warm gold accent. The upper area remains visually quiet for the manually added headline, but the generated image itself contains no text.",
    "first_frame_scene": "Begin closer than the thumbnail: an almost abstract black knot fills the center of the frame beneath the recurring figure's hand. The knot subtly resembles a compressed shadow rather than a literal organ. Around it, off-white chalk lines reveal the figure's round head and rigid shoulders. A narrow vertical reflection of warm gold appears on the window glass at the edge of frame, with no visible successful person yet. The composition is quiet, tense, and text-free.",
    "first_15s_visuals": [
      "0-3 seconds: Hold on the chest knot and the hand pressing against it. The polite smile is only partially visible above the frame, creating immediate contradiction without copying the thumbnail.",
      "3-6 seconds: The camera slowly pulls back to reveal the recurring figure standing beside the window. The figure's shadow is slightly larger than the body and begins sliding across the sill toward the gold reflection.",
      "6-9 seconds: The window reflection briefly shows an anonymous silhouette surrounded by restrained gold light, but the reflection is indistinct and never becomes a literal celebratory scene. The figure remains in the foreground, looking toward it.",
      "9-12 seconds: The figure lowers the hand from the chest, but the black knot remains suspended as a shadow-shaped mark on the clothing, suggesting that suppressing the reaction has not removed it.",
      "12-15 seconds: The gold reflection narrows into a small opening while the oversized shadow reaches toward it. End on the window as a psychological boundary, establishing the visual question of whether the painful reaction points only outward or also toward an unacknowledged possibility within the self."
    ]
  }
}
