rt of the same self.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":false,"reuse_image_id":"C03-B13"},{"id":"C03-B15","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The recurring figure places one hand against the clouded mirror and a single narrow gold glint appears along the existing crack; it marks a first moment of recognizing excluded emotion.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B16","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The mirror haze thins around the figure’s lowered reflection while the gold glint remains small and contained; it shows recognition without turning the shadow into an independent entity.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":false,"reuse_image_id":"C03-B15"},{"id":"C03-B17","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The outer figure and its reflection face one another across the mirror with matching rounded heads and continuous contours; it represents vulnerable feelings being acknowledged as part of the whole person.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B18","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The figure lowers its reassuring hand and stands quietly beside the clearer reflection; it prepares the transition from rejecting difficult feelings toward recognizing the pain caused by their separation.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":false,"reuse_image_id":"C03-B17"}]}
