ed fragments and grows heavier beside the figure, still physically attached. Visualize how unacknowledged aspects remain active outside conscious self-understanding.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B15","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The figure stands inside a clean chalk outline while the old photograph and shadow remain beyond its boundary. Show the protective clarity of a present persona becoming restrictive.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B16","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The clean outline closes into a narrow paper enclosure, while the shadow presses against its outer edge. Depict reduced self-understanding caused by excluding difficult history.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B17","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The figure looks between the photograph and the shadow, lowering the covering hand without touching either. Mark the beginning of observation instead of immediate judgment.","mode":"literal","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B18","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The figure places the photograph beside the attached shadow on the same off-white paper field, with the thin gold thread still unbroken. Show the denied image becoming available for understanding.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C03-B19","script_section":"S3","visual_information":"The present silhouette, old photograph imprint, and shadow form one restrained composition with a small open space between them. Conclude that the shadow names an unplaced aspect of personal history, not a verdict that the past self was bad.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null}]}
