l},{"id":"C04-B08","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure sits on the off-white threshold with one fist hidden against its body; unspoken resentment is shown as an internal cost of repeated accommodation.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B09","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The closed door and the seated figure share the same frame, with the gold seam faintly visible; the boundary exists even though the figure has not voiced it.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B10","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure rises and places one palm against the door without opening it; recognizing a limit is separated from attacking or abandoning the other person.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B11","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The black mass behind the door recedes slightly while the figure’s outline becomes clearer; reduced pressure allows the hidden refusal to become part of awareness.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B12","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure stands between the door and open paper space, with the clenched hand slowly loosening; anger and fatigue are acknowledged without being acted out destructively.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B13","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The figure faces the closed door from a small distance instead of holding it shut; a boundary can preserve contact without requiring automatic agreement.","mode":"metaphor","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null},{"id":"C04-B14","script_section":"S4","visual_information":"The recurring figure remains beside the closed door with a clearer chalk outline and a restrained gold seam; integration reframes kindness as a choice rather than proof of goodness.","mode":"symbolic","new_image":true,"reuse_image_id":null}]}
